Margo Wren
14 Harbour Lane, Port Ellis

PAGE ONE (two panels)

Panel 1. A lighthouse on a cliff at dusk. Maya climbs the last of the steps.

MAYA:
Theo? The lamp is out --

Panel 2. Inside. Theo kneels by the dead lamp, his tools around him.

THEO (whisper):
-- because somebody forgot the oil.

MAYA (thought):
Somebody.

PAGE TWO (one panel)

Panel One. The lamp blazes. Both of them squint against it.

SFX:
FWOOMP

THEO:
There. Now it is lit.

PAGE THREE (two panels)

Panel 1. The beam sweeps the water.

CAP:
Three nights later.

1. MAYA (burst):
THEO!

2. THEO: I'm here --
-- I'm here.

Panel 2. A boat on the rocks, far below.
@over: 1

CAP/MAYA
“-- and that was how we found it.”

THEO (V.O.)
Nobody believed us.

KEEPER (OP, right):
Who's up there?
